-- Migration 54: first-class `aliases` array on entity (Phase K.3)
--
-- Track K.3's retroactive canonicalization collapses fragmented entities
-- (`BZK` / `ministerie van BZK` / `Binnenlandse Zaken...`) into one canonical
-- winner. On merge, each loser's surface form is recorded both as an
-- `entity_alias` edge (migration 39 — authoritative, per-alias provenance) AND
-- denormalized onto the winner's `aliases` array for cheap read/display and
-- exporter use (decision K-D1: keep both, the table is authoritative, the array
-- is derived). K.4/K.6 read this array.
--
-- `status` ('active' | 'merged' | 'archived') and `merged_into` already exist
-- on `entity` from migration 39 (lines 38-39), as does the status index
-- (`idx_entity_status`, migration 39 line 46) — so K.3 only needs to add the
-- `aliases` field here. The DEFINE statements below are written defensively with
-- IF NOT EXISTS so re-applying on a DB that already carries them is a no-op.
--
-- B.8 caution: the `entity` table carries pre-Track-B schema drift (migration 50
-- relaxed `name`/`hash_id`/`entity_type`). This migration is ADDITIVE only —
-- `IF NOT EXISTS`, never OVERWRITE — and does NOT touch `canonical_name`,
-- `hash_id`, or `entity_type`, so the B.8 dedup-key / upsert contract is intact.
--
-- Additive + idempotent: the new field has a safe default (`[]`) so pre-existing
-- rows read back unchanged, and IF NOT EXISTS makes re-run a no-op. The B.0
-- testcontainers roundtrip harness validates this by replaying the migration.

DEFINE FIELD IF NOT EXISTS aliases ON entity FLEXIBLE TYPE array DEFAULT [];

-- `status` + `merged_into` are defined in migration 39 (the entity table is
-- SCHEMAFULL). Re-declare defensively with IF NOT EXISTS so a database that
-- somehow lost them (drift) regains them WITHOUT overwriting the migration-39
-- definitions on a normal DB. Same for the status index used to filter
-- active/merged entities efficiently during retroactive merge.
DEFINE FIELD IF NOT EXISTS status ON entity TYPE string DEFAULT 'active';
DEFINE FIELD IF NOT EXISTS merged_into ON entity TYPE option<string>;
DEFINE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_entity_status ON entity FIELDS status;
